From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: defer live RRO recovery until consumers stop

RRO session release runs while Wi-Fi packet producers and DMA remain
active. Do not reboot the NPU inline when a fresh-slot mailbox health
check fails: software recovery does not establish a consumer DMA fence.

Propagate the health-check error to the existing RRO worker. It retains
session ownership and schedules full Wi-Fi recovery, which stops the
consumers before rebooting the NPU and replaying its configuration.
Keep the no-reboot mailbox health-check retry when it succeeds.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
diff --git a/npu.c b/npu.c
index fadd40d..74ebec9 100644
--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -516,13 +516,10 @@
 	if (err == -EAGAIN)
 		err = airoha_npu_wait_recovery(npu);
 	else if (err == -ETIMEDOUT) {
+		/* A live RRO release must leave a failed mailbox recovery to
+		 * the caller, which stops consumers before rebooting the NPU.
+		 */
 		err = airoha_npu_recover_mailbox(npu);
-		if (err) {
-			dev_warn(dev->dev,
-				 "NPU mailbox health check failed: %d; forcing recovery\n",
-				 err);
-			err = airoha_npu_recover(npu);
-		}
 	}
 
 	if (retry && !err)
